{"title":"2007 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<div style=\"float:right\">\n<p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2007_CyMO-15.PNG\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/9/94/2007_CyMO-15.PNG/250px-2007_CyMO-15.PNG\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"250\" height=\"243\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/9/94/2007_CyMO-15.PNG/375px-2007_CyMO-15.PNG 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/9/94/2007_CyMO-15.PNG/500px-2007_CyMO-15.PNG 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<p>The reflex angles of the concave octagon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/5/055dcba798b1424c44c2606d913e0f2edab1c5ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDEFGH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"120\" height=\"14\" /> measure <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/c/8dc634edb1f6435bb03e5759545d8d142ac8653b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$240^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" /> each. Diagonals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a65c05bd85d2609bea5db2b109ed5f556463511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/e/68ebf9f9ddef66e02f09fcf82b59f6c54ec2bb33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GC$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> are perpendicular, bisect each other, and are both equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>The area of the octagon is \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/f/e0f8cc2ca5da69aeac24ee8b36f65777e9295e24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A) \\ } \\frac{6-2\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ } 8\\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\ } 1\\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\ } \\frac{6+2\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\ } \\mathrm{None\\;of\\;these}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"559\" height=\"41\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The problem statement apparently misses one crucial piece of information: the fact that <b>all the sides of the octagon are equal</b>. Without this fact the octagon area is not uniquely determined. For example, we could move point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> along a suitable arc (the locus of all points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/3/a83f718b5548bdac1f5c7a32217941c1c739ebef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AXC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/f/f3fd424e953ac76b50bf6103875acc049d21d3c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$120^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" />), and as this would change the height from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, it would change the area of the triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, and hence the area of the octagon.\n</p><p>With this additional assumption we can compute the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/5/055dcba798b1424c44c2606d913e0f2edab1c5ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDEFGH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"120\" height=\"14\" /> as the area of the square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/7/577991bfcbdc9404a5871bae06764c4785c7048a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACEG$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> (which is obviously <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />), minus four times the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/f/08fffa12a15c5d89c9d9775b181e8291d6b6659b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(4cm); defaultpen(0.8); pair a=(0,1), c=(1,0), bb=(a+c)/2, b=bb+dir(225)/sqrt(6); draw (a -- b -- c -- cycle); draw (a -- (0,0) -- c); draw (b -- bb); label (&quot;$A$&quot;, a, N ); label (&quot;$B$&quot;, b, SW ); label (&quot;$C$&quot;, c, S ); label (&quot;$B&#39;$&quot;, bb, NE ); label (&quot;$1$&quot;, a/2, W ); [/asy]\" width=\"218\" height=\"235\" />\n</p><p>In the triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/3/023b860b0eefa5e558a04188f82a5bd47ea37e1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=\\sqrt 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/7/4c71f19552a05ee5e2b31e94aff3fb986884bf31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B&#39;$\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the foot of the height from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> onto <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/4/5f4c25cb7b6078137512af0317bd262160bd0319.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=BC$\" width=\"81\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/7/4c71f19552a05ee5e2b31e94aff3fb986884bf31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B&#39;$\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> bisects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. As the angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/f/f3fd424e953ac76b50bf6103875acc049d21d3c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$120^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" />, the angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/a/74a48760ced9fbfbbf84cff69d7d094425db8399.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABB&#39;$\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/f/29fa0a9949f018e121b2093216dd5db13d3abef0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>We now have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/c/c4cf0d20ccaaa68e2f67ea9e10912ae7a005e393.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AB&#39;}{BB&#39;} = \\tan 60^\\circ = \\sqrt 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"166\" height=\"38\" />. Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/c/b0cfdb20013b8c7f7436b21cfa564592b602756b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BB&#39;=\\frac{AB&#39;}{\\sqrt 3} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt 6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"146\" height=\"42\" />.\n</p><p>Then the area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9865981e8692da062e9ea0882a2c72c5ddd51c28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{BB&#39; \\cdot AC}2 = \\frac{\\sqrt 2}{2\\sqrt 6} = \\frac 1{2\\sqrt 3} = \\frac{\\sqrt 3}6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"253\" height=\"45\" />.\n</p><p>Hence the area of the given octogon is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/3/473766871995820253d8995d3dfe967cc30944fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 - 4\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt 3}6 = \\boxed{\\frac{6 - 2\\sqrt 3}3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"186\" height=\"53\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; align:center; width:60%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum\" title=\"2007 Cyprus MO/Lyceum\">2007 Cyprus MO, Lyceum</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problems\" title=\"2007 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problems\">Problems</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_14\" title=\"2007 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_16\" title=\"2007 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_1\" title=\"2007 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_2\" title=\"2007 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_3\" title=\"2007 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_4\" title=\"2007 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_5\" title=\"2007 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_6\" title=\"2007 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_7\" title=\"2007 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_8\" title=\"2007 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_9\" title=\"2007 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_10\" title=\"2007 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_11\" title=\"2007 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_12\" title=\"2007 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_13\" title=\"2007 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_14\" title=\"2007 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_16\" title=\"2007 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_17\" title=\"2007 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_18\" title=\"2007 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_19\" title=\"2007 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_20\" title=\"2007 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_21\" title=\"2007 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_22\" title=\"2007 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_23\" title=\"2007 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_24\" title=\"2007 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_25\" title=\"2007 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 25\">25</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_26\" title=\"2007 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 26\">26</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_27\" title=\"2007 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 27\">27</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_28\" title=\"2007 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 28\">28</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_29\" title=\"2007 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 29\">29</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_30\" title=\"2007 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 30\">30</a>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018053214\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.035 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.054 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 275/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2045/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 358/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6637/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.459      1 Template:CYMO_box\n100.00%    7.459      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:4941:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018053214 and revision id 29812. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}